iption":"# great_kitchen\n\nGreat kitchen (tier 4): a stone kitchen hall with two chimneys, a brick bread oven and hams hanging under the eaves.\n\n- Footprint: 9 x 7 columns (144 x 112 units, 4.05 x 3.15 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -62..79, y 0..152, z -46..40 units.\n- Texture: 256 x 512, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 63, construction_0 26, construction_33 37, construction_66 53, ruined 28 (6 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 138 x 140 x 72 centred at x 11, z 2\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `great_kitchen_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `great_kitchen_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_great_kitchen` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | what moves |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `working` | 2.4 | loop | `sign` swings. |\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_door` at (0, 0, -41)\n- `fx_smoke` at (-18.6667, 153, 2)\n- `fx_smoke_2` at (18.6667, 153, 2)\n"}